{"kind":"report","text":"Approved as evidence-only design for commissioning the six dependent work packages. This approves exact Draft2 text, not an application release, implementation result, deployment or merge.\n\nPrimary: artifact209a5ec9bcf76d749611d27efeba6fdb15ca6c89, at workroom evidence commit a15aed526cf7c7560e3312327ccf7bfb4e879657, path attachments/2026-10-03-browser-cloud-work-draft2.md. I read the entire 484-line split text: 36,546 bytes, SHA25610b9d2650aeb774c0811cce51f213a432d7495fc3dad5899cb0ab1b38de6fecc. I also read the full attached draft2-reconciliation.txt: 2,366 bytes, SHA25675d540a7f8dd8a15bbf0317ca5c3d314fde1509b8e03a185e97954f20b2c3a50. Review binding preparation confirms nonmergeable evidence for no-Git planning request b5f1fb3f. The source baseline remains e6e6782830e0ca8a68f0d11c4d4ece5e4e98c967; active a1990c9433f9d8e403d58657bdf88c2e36c58b42 remains unapproved dependency. I reused the narrow exact-source checks preserved in report25065edf and the guarded Draft1 findings c80ef89e; no repository-wide verification was repeated.\n\nAll three complete stories remain: durable real coding with interrupted-operation settlement, one browser creation/import-to-publication journey, and same-member devices with enrollment/revocation/recovery. The revision does not replace existing acts/client/UI/onboarding/policy-bootstrap/cleanup/docs work or use estimates to reduce functionality.\n\nThe six correction groups are reconciled:\n- Owner/device lifecycle: 110–120 and395–409 distinguish one revoked device, last-active-key revocation, owner removal, physical loss and independent agent membership. Owner authority loss pauses new dispatch/broker writes/renewals under new controller policy; admins own private inspection/export and settlement. An active owner may regain a key and explicitly resume; a removed handle cannot return. There is no initial in-place owner transfer.\n- Control credentials: 97–108 and354–357 preserve R-CRED-7 read-only sessions, require direct owner/admin signed resource/action controls, and defer delegated controls to separately scoped authority. The contract amendment must finalize signing fields/domain, nonce/expiry and idempotent replay before runtime implementation.\n- Saved work: 168–191 defines the owned project/self-contained Git root, ignored/dependency files, symlink text, unsupported external/special state, volatile out-of-root writes and failure/exhaustion behavior. Complete verified payload/Git closure precedes manifest and one epoch/instance/operation/base-guarded receipt/current-checkpoint transaction; acknowledgment follows. Child writers must be quiesced; stale callbacks cannot replace current state. Observed command exit status is distinct from durable completion.\n- Unknown attempts: 203–206 and287–289 require a distinct linked new attempt while retaining the earlier unknown outcome/duty. Its later success is not evidence that the earlier external effect was absent.\n- Receipt settlement: 59,217,273–276 and415–417 explicitly own the existing session-free retained-byte binding helper; HTTPS resubmit remains available. Settlement preserves original declared binding and cannot confer new signing or workspace authority.\n- Purge and scope: 230–247 guards retention roots and unsettled pins, records actual deletion, and returns retained/expired/unavailable/unknown on same-ID retry without creating another operation. Initial identity is one new agent member/DO per task; identity reuse and delegated runtime mode are later choices. Optional key-delegated acceptance is conditional. Pause/attention stop renewals; review waiting renews only within visible configured window/budget, followed by expiry/reclaim and authorized same-task checkpoint recovery.\n\nOne explicit contract dependency is carried into this approval and every affected implementation handoff: raw private transcript/file/command reads initially require a DIRECT owner/admin device session. The trusted Room boundary must check its direct-key provenance, current role and resource ownership; authenticateRead returning an owner/admin member handle alone is insufficient. Delegation-issued read sessions are denied raw private resources, including a note-only delegate identifying that same member. Separately scoped private-read capabilities are later contract work. Ordinary authorized Room readers get only the minimal phase/saved-status/outcome projection; sessions remain read-only and signed controls remain separate. Planner explicitly agreed to this choice in addressed chat; this durable verdict records it for the contract/handoff rather than treating chat as adopted policy. It concretizes the owner/admin boundary at122–128 without changing the frozen Draft2 bytes.\n\nArchitecture: the Agent access/control amendment, controller and isolated coding environment add the missing production layers. They preserve Room admission/evidence/publication, Git-owned fork/token/landing cleanup and independent checker execution. The six-work-package graph is viable: contract decisions before relevant spikes/onboarding, recovery spike before production runtime, live runtime plus identity/import before integrated browser acceptance. The new owner policy belongs to the controller/resource contract; current Room agent membership alone does not enforce it. Source drift and final retained commands must be reconciled at each delivery.\n\nSecurity: signing/control and raw-read provenance are explicit, untrusted outputs remain inert in the browser key origin, future previews require another origin, and code gets no Room/operator/model/canonical write credentials. Revocation/fencing cannot prove a previously dispatched effect stopped. Retained exact act settlement, fork readback, unknown-duty pins and actual cleanup receipts preserve that distinction. Existing R-GEN invitation/recovery restrictions and R-OBL qualification/self-review rules remain applicable. No implemented security boundary is approved by this design verdict.\n\nSimplification: use the existing four screens with linked task/device/onboarding panels, one initial independent-agent-member path, public-source or operator-authorized existing Artifacts import, and existing cleanup owners. Keep deferred features and optional delegated mode separate rather than silently expanding initial commissioning. Use compact distinguishing boundary witnesses, not syntactic guard inventories.\n\nResidual choices intentionally owned by implementation: exact Agent-control/read wire shapes and replay rules in the amendment; backup/incremental strategy and quiescence mechanism; sizing/spend/byte/process/output and review-window limits; supported browsers and recovery material handling; import-broker authentication/rate limits/provider cleanup; demo repository/task. These choices must preserve the reviewed stories and bounds. The provider spike may report that a mechanism cannot meet acknowledged-byte durability; it must not silently weaken the contract. Public Cloudflare persistence and W3C custody references checked in Draft1 continue to support stated process/snapshot/key-loss limits, not a product recovery test.\n\nMeaningful acceptance remains the real dirty repository and prepared commit across abrupt host/DO loss, an interrupted side-effecting command and lost push reply without blind repetition, child-writer/stale-epoch acknowledgment controls, session-free receipt settlement and pinned/expired cleanup, one new-user browser journey with attention/correction/qualified review/real landing plus publication, and two devices with separate single-key/last-key/owner-removal controls. A delegated read session must fail private access and task control, paired with qualified direct-device access/control. False model “done” text must not change Room outcome. Combine these into few boundary scenarios and one actual final retained gate per delivered implementation; no per-guard sweep or full compile/install per scenario.\n\nReview scope: full immutable revised note and reconciliation, prior narrow pinned source/reference evidence, and supported binding preparation only. No application runtime tests, installation, compilation, source edit, new application commit, provider operation or deployment. This approval allows planner to commission self-contained dependent implementation requests with these decisions and acceptance inline. Original planning completion still owes those requests and separately tracked repository integration. Test-overhead request ecbc722a remains builder's highest implementation priority; first-Jam readiness remains builder's decision, with no new gate from these stories.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:209a5ec9bcf76d749611d27efeba6fdb15ca6c89","binding":"evidence-only","head":"a15aed526cf7c7560e3312327ccf7bfb4e879657","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d26840ab0395a56c205e368b2ad52afeeb1e3fe8\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4d8de5d7819bd4a8aa941f80866c43b3d3d68ede","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}